
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

  <title>Baltimore Heat Wave Data Visualizations</title>

  <link
    href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
    rel="stylesheet">

  <style>
    body {
      background-color: #f8f9fa;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      background: white;
      padding: 35px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-weight: bold;
      color: #292929;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 24px;
      margin-top: 35px;
      color: #333;
    }

    .source {
      color: #666;
      font-size: 14px;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    iframe {
      width: 100%;
      border: none;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <div class="container my-5">

    <h1>Baltimore Heat Wave Data Visualizations</h1>

    <p>
      Exploring extreme heat, indoor and outdoor temperatures,
      and heat-related deaths in Baltimore and Maryland.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <!-- FIRST GRAPH: LINE CHART -->

    <h2>
      Indoor and outdoor heat index during Baltimore heat wave,
      July 16-22, 2019
    </h2>

    <iframe
      title="Indoor and outdoor heat index"
      src="https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/yRI0U/1/"
      height="500"
      scrolling="no">
    </iframe>

    <p class="source">
      Source: Federal government weather data via Iowa State University
      and indoor temperature data captured by University of Maryland journalists.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <!-- SECOND GRAPH: BAR CHART -->

    <h2>
      Baltimore has more than its share of heat-related deaths in Maryland
    </h2>

    <iframe
      title="Hot weather deaths in Baltimore and Maryland"
      src="https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/7tBEb/1/"
      height="500"
      scrolling="no">
    </iframe>

    <p class="source">
      Source: Maryland Department of Health.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <footer class="text-muted">
      <p>Baltimore Heat Wave Data Visualization Project</p>
    </footer>

  </div>

</body>
</html>
